 ## Overview
-Coordinate Grid Generation produces a structured set of spatial coordinates (typically in Normalized Device Coordinates, NDC, range $[-1, 1]$) that align with the discrete sampling grid of a volume or image. It solves the problem of mapping integer pixel or voxel indices to continuous physical or normalized space for neural field training, ray casting, and SDF evaluation. It differs from its sibling [Rasterization-based Voxelization](908-rasterization-based-voxelization.md) by generating the *sample points* themselves rather than determining *which* voxels a primitive occupies, and from [3D Coordinate Grid Generation](2333-3d-coordinate-grid-generation.md) by primarily targeting 2D image-plane coordinates for ray origin generation, though it extends to 3D.
