 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Even vs Odd Dimensions:** The normalization formula $\frac{x - (W-1)/2}{(W-1)/2}$ ensures the center pixel (at index $(W-1)/2$) maps to 0. If $W$ is even, the center falls between pixels, which is standard for NDC but may require careful handling in ray origins [S4, unofficial].
