 ### [3D Coordinate Grid Generation](2333-3d-coordinate-grid-generation.md)
-Generates a 3D grid of sample points within a voxel space for Signed Distance Function (SDF) evaluation. It produces a set of 3D points forming a regular grid within a unit cube, typically excluding boundary regions to ensure samples lie strictly inside the volume. It differs from its parent [Coordinate Grid Generation](1273-coordinate-grid-generation.md) by explicitly mapping integer grid indices to continuous 3D coordinates in world space (often $[-1, 1]$) using voxel size and origin parameters, rather than generating normalized 2D image coordinates.
+Generates a 3D grid of sample points within a voxel space for Signed Distance Function (SDF) evaluation. It produces a set of 3D points forming a regular grid within a unit cube, typically excluding boundary regions to ensure samples lie strictly inside the volume. It differs from its parent [Coordinate Grid Generation](1273-coordinate-grid-generation.md) by explicitly mapping integer grid indices to continuous 3D coordinates in world space (often $[-1, 1]$) using voxel size and origin parameters, rather than generating normalized 2D image coordinates [G].
 
 ### Meshgrid XY
-Mimics `np.meshgrid(..., indexing="xy")` in PyTorch, as `torch.meshgrid` only allows `"ij"` indexing [S6, unofficial]. It is chosen when compatibility with NumPy's coordinate layout is required. The implementation calls `torch.meshgrid(tensor1, tensor2)` and returns `ii.transpose(-1, -2), jj.transpose(-1, -2)` [S6, unofficial].
