+- **Strengths:** Provides exact, differentiable coordinate mappings essential for neural rendering and SDF optimization [S2, unofficial][S5, unofficial].
 - **Limitations:** Memory usage grows cubically for 3D grids, limiting resolution for dense volumes [G].
 
 ## Background
-Coordinate grid generation is a fundamental preprocessing step in neural radiance fields (NeRF) and implicit surface representations. It originated with the need to sample input coordinates for multi-layer perceptrons (MLPs) that map spatial positions to color and density [S1, S2, unofficial]. The $[-1, 1]$ NDC convention is widely adopted in computer graphics for camera space normalization [S4, unofficial].
